(CHAPTER I) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PRESIDENTIAL RECONSTRUCTION) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The question, what political disposition should be made of the Confederate) Tj T*
(States after the destruction of their military power, began to be) Tj T*
(prominent in public discussion in December, 1863. It was then that) Tj T*
(President Lincoln announced his policy upon the subject, which was to) Tj T*
(restore each state to its former position in the Union as soon as) Tj T*
(one-tenth of its population had taken the oath of allegiance prescribed in) Tj T*
(his amnesty proclamation and had organized a state government pledged to) Tj T*
(abolish slavery. This policy Lincoln applied to those states which were) Tj T*
(subdued by the federal forces during his administration, viz., Tennessee,) Tj T*
(Arkansas and Louisiana. When the remaining states of the Confederacy) Tj T*
(surrendered in 1865, President Johnson applied the same policy, with some) Tj T*
ET
