(and the commanders sometimes removed the civil officers and appointed) Tj T*
(others, sometimes allowed them to remain, subject to their direction.) Tj T*
(Military orders were issued regarding a wide range of civil affairs, such) Tj T*
(as school administration, sanitary provisions, the regulation of trade,) Tj T*
(the fixing of prices at which commodities should be sold, etc.[7] The) Tj T*
(provost marshal's courts were further useful, to some extent, as) Tj T*
(substitutes for the state courts, whose operations were largely) Tj T*
(interrupted.[8] Directions to the officers of the Department admonished) Tj T*
(them that "the military authority should sustain, not assume the functions) Tj T*
(of, civil authority," except when the latter course was necessary to) Tj T*
(preserve the peace.[9] This admonition from headquarters, issued after the) Tj T*
(President's plan for reinstating Georgia in the Union had been put into) Tj T*
(operation, reflects his desire for a quick restoration of normal) Tj T*
(government.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(President Johnson announced his policy toward the seceded states in his) Tj T*
(proclamation of May 29, 1865, regarding North Carolina. By it a) Tj T*
(provisional governor was appointed for that state, with the duty of making) Tj T*
(the necessary arrangements for the meeting of a constitutional convention,) Tj T*
(to be composed of and elected by men who had taken the oath of allegiance) Tj T*
(prescribed by, the President's amnesty proclamation of the same date, and) Tj T*
(who were qualified voters according to the laws of the state in force) Tj T*
(before the war. The proclamation did not state what the President would) Tj T*
(require of the convention, but we may mention by way of anticipation that) Tj T*
(his requirements were the revocation of the ordinance of secession, the) Tj T*
(construction of a new state government in place of the rebel government,) Tj T*
(the repudiation of the rebel debt, and the abolition of slavery within the) Tj T*
(state. The provisional governor was further authorized to do whatever was) Tj T*
("necessary and proper to enable [the] loyal people of the state of North) Tj T*
(Carolina to restore said state to its constitutional relations to the) Tj T*
(federal government."[10]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For each of the states subdued in 1865, except Virginia, a provisional) Tj T*
(governor was appointed by a similar proclamation. On June 17, James) Tj T*
(Johnson, a citizen of Georgia, was appointed to the position in that) Tj T*
(state.[11] On July 13th, he issued a proclamation providing for the) Tj T*
(election of the convention. Delegates were distributed on the basis of the) Tj T*
(legislature of 1860; the first Wednesday in October was set for the) Tj T*
(election, and the fourth Wednesday in the same month for the meeting of) Tj T*
(the convention.[12] Next, the provisional governor undertook the task of) Tj T*
(securing popular support to the programme of restoration. To encourage) Tj T*
(subscription to the amnesty oath \(a prerequisite to voting for delegates) Tj T*
(to the convention\) he removed the disagreeable necessity of taking it) Tj T*
(before the military authorities by directing the ordinary and the clerk of) Tj T*
(the Superior Court of each county to administer it.[13] He made many) Tj T*
(speeches throughout the state urging the citizens to take the amnesty) Tj T*
(oath, to enter earnestly into the election of the convention, and to) Tj T*
(submit quietly to the conditions imposed by the President.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(His efforts were very successful. This was partly due to the place he held) Tj T*
(in public estimation. He was a lawyer widely known and universally) Tj T*
(respected. It was also partly due to the attitude of Governor Brown.) Tj T*
ET
