(Brown, after a confinement of several weeks in prison at Washington,) Tj T*
(secured an interview with President Johnson, and satisfied the President) Tj T*
(that his object in calling the legislature was simply public relief, that) Tj T*
(he had no intention to prolong the war, but calmly submitted to the fact) Tj T*
(that his side was defeated.[14] This explanation and the spirit displayed) Tj T*
(were so satisfactory to Johnson that Brown was released, and permitted to) Tj T*
(return to Georgia. His return, remarked Johnson, "can be turned to good) Tj T*
(account. He will at once go to work and do all he can in restoring the) Tj T*
(state."[15] This prediction proved correct. The war governor of Georgia) Tj T*
(became the type of those Secessionists who practised and counseled quiet) Tj T*
(acceptance of the terms imposed by the conqueror, as the most sensible and) Tj T*
(advantageous course. On June 29th he issued an address to the people of) Tj T*
(Georgia, resigning the governorship, and advising acquiescence in the) Tj T*
(abolition of slavery and active participation in the reorganization of the) Tj T*
(state government according to the President's wishes.[16] The assumption) Tj T*
(of this attitude by Brown grieved and offended some of his fellow) Tj T*
(Secessionists. But the majority shared his opinion. The provisional) Tj T*
(governor was welcomed, and his speeches approved on all sides.[17] The) Tj T*
(result was that the convention which met on October 25th was a body) Tj T*
(distinguished for the reputation and ability of its members.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The convention was called to order by the provisional governor, and chose) Tj T*
(as permanent chairman Herschel V. Johnson.[18] Then a message from the) Tj T*
(provisional governor was read, suggesting certain measures of finance and) Tj T*
(other state business requiring immediate action, suggesting also certain) Tj T*
(alterations in the state judiciary, but especially pointing out the chief) Tj T*
(objects of the convention, viz., the passage of those acts requisite for) Tj T*
(the restoration of the state.[19] These measures the convention quickly) Tj T*
(proceeded to pass. On October 26th it repealed the ordinance of secession) Tj T*
(and the ordinance ratifying the Confederate constitution;[20] by paragraph) Tj T*
(20 of article I. of the new constitution it abolished slavery in the) Tj T*
(state; and on November 8th, the last day of the session, it declared the) Tj T*
(state debt contracted to aid the Confederacy void.[21] The convention) Tj T*
(provided for a general state election on the following November 15th, and) Tj T*
(to expedite complete restoration, anticipated the regular work of the) Tj T*
(legislature by creating congressional districts, in order that Georgia's) Tj T*
(representatives might be chosen at that election.[22]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One thing now remained to be done before the President would withdraw) Tj T*
(federal power and leave the state to its own government, viz.,) Tj T*
(ratification of the Thirteenth Amendment. The legislature elected on) Tj T*
(November 15th assembled on December 4th.[23] The provisional governor,) Tj T*
(according to the President's directions,[24] laid the Thirteenth Amendment) Tj T*
(before it. The Amendment was ratified on December 9th.[25] After this the) Tj T*
(provisional governor was relieved, the governor elect was inaugurated) Tj T*
(\(December 14th\), and the President sent a courteous message of recognition) Tj T*
(to the latter.[26]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Thus the President, having reconstructed the state government, had) Tj T*
(restored Georgia to statehood so far as its internal government was) Tj T*
(concerned. There remained only the admission of its representatives to) Tj T*
(Congress to complete the restoration.) Tj T*
ET
