(     [were] murdering the loyal whites daily, and daily putting into) Tj T*
(     secret graves not only hundreds but thousands of the colored) Tj T*
(     people.[68]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At first the lower house resumed its consideration of the bills) Tj T*
(recommended at the last session by the joint committee. But early in) Tj T*
(February, 1867, these were dropped in favor of a new bill. This was the) Tj T*
(Reconstruction Bill which became law on March 2. It provided that the) Tj T*
(South should be divided into five districts, each to comprise the) Tj T*
(territory of one or more of the southern states. The President should) Tj T*
(assign to each district a military officer not below the rank of) Tj T*
(brigadier-general, and should detail for his use a sufficient military) Tj T*
(force. The duties of these officers should be "to protect all persons in) Tj T*
(their rights of person and property, to suppress insurrection, disorder) Tj T*
(and violence, and to punish, or cause to be punished, disturbers of the) Tj T*
(public peace and criminals." To this end they might either allow local) Tj T*
(courts to exercise their usual jurisdiction or organize special military) Tj T*
(courts, for the procedure of which a few general regulations were provided) Tj T*
(in the bill. Until the states should be by law restored to the Union, the) Tj T*
(governments existing in them were declared "provisional only, and in all) Tj T*
(respects subject to the paramount authority of the United States, at any) Tj T*
(time to abolish, modify, control or suspend the same.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In section 5 of this bill were stated the conditions upon which the) Tj T*
(southern states might regain their places in the Union. In each of them a) Tj T*
(constitutional convention should be elected. For members of this) Tj T*
(convention all male "citizens" of the voting age should vote, except those) Tj T*
