() Tj T*
(CHAPTER IV) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE ADMINISTRATIONS OF POPE AND MEADE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the Third Military District, of which Georgia was a part, the) Tj T*
(Reconstruction Acts were administered from April 1, 1867, to January 6,) Tj T*
(1868, by General Pope, and from January 6 to July 30, 1868, by General) Tj T*
(Meade.[82] The present chapter will describe, first, the manner in which) Tj T*
(these men conducted the political rebuilding of Georgia, and second, the) Tj T*
(manner in which they governed during this process.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On April 8 Pope issued his first orders regarding the registration of) Tj T*
(voters. The three officers commanding respectively in the sub-districts of) Tj T*
(Georgia, Florida and Alabama were directed to divide the territory under) Tj T*
(them into registration districts, and for each of these to appoint a board) Tj T*
(of registry consisting as far as possible of civilians.[83] On May 2 the) Tj T*
(scheme of districts for Georgia was published. The state was divided into) Tj T*
(forty-four districts of three counties each, and three districts of a city) Tj T*
(each. For each district the names of two white registrars were announced,) Tj T*
