(and each of these pairs was ordered to complete the board by selecting a) Tj T*
(negro colleague. The compensation of registrars was to be from fifteen) Tj T*
(cents to forty cents for every name registered, varying according to the) Tj T*
(density or sparseness of the population. It was made the duty of) Tj T*
(registrars to explain to those unused to the enjoyment of suffrage the) Tj T*
(nature of this function. After the lists were complete they were to be) Tj T*
(published for ten days.[84]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The unsettled condition of the negro population suggested to Pope the) Tj T*
(possibility that many negroes would lose their right to vote by change of) Tj T*
(residence. He therefore ordered on August 15 that persons removing from) Tj T*
(the district where they were registered should be furnished by the board) Tj T*
(of registry with a certificate of registration, which should entitle them) Tj T*
(to vote anywhere in the state.[85]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The election for deciding whether a constitutional convention should be) Tj T*
(held, and for choosing delegates in case the affirmative vote prevailed,) Tj T*
(was ordered to begin on October 29 and to continue three days. Registrars) Tj T*
(were ordered to revise their lists during the fortnight preceding the) Tj T*
(election, to erase names wrongly registered, and to add the names of) Tj T*
(persons entitled to be registered. The boards of registry were to act as) Tj T*
(judges of election, but registrars who were candidates for election were) Tj T*
(forbidden to serve in the districts where they sought election.[86]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The election was to occupy the last three days of October. On October 30) Tj T*
(Pope extended the time to the night of November 2, in order to give the) Tj T*
(negroes ample opportunity to vote, which in their inexperience they might) Tj T*
(otherwise fail to do.[87]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After the election the following figures were announced:[88]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  Number of registered voters in Georgia      188,647) Tj T*
(  Of these the negroes numbered                93,457) Tj T*
(       "   the white men[89]                   95,214) Tj T*
(  Number of votes polled                      106,410) Tj T*
(    "       "     for a convention            102,283) Tj T*
(    "       "     against a convention          4,127) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The delegates elected were ordered to meet in convention on December) Tj T*
(9th.[90] On that day the convention met in Atlanta. Its business was not) Tj T*
(completed until the middle of March in the following year. The) Tj T*
(constitution which it framed more than met the demands of the) Tj T*
(Reconstruction Acts. A single citizenship was established for all) Tj T*
(residents of the state, in language borrowed from the Fourteenth Amendment) Tj T*
(to the federal Constitution.[91] Legislation on the subject of social) Tj T*
(status of citizens was forever prohibited.[92] The electoral right was) Tj T*
(given to all male persons born or naturalized in the United States who) Tj T*
(should have resided six months in Georgia.[93] Electors were privileged) Tj T*
(from arrest \(except for treason, felony or breach of the peace\) for five) Tj T*
(days before, during, and for two days after, elections, and the) Tj T*
(legislature was ordered to provide such other means for the protection of) Tj T*
(electors as might be necessary.[94] Other provisions presumably acceptable) Tj T*
