(       *       *       *       *       *) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(General Pope was inspired by the ideas and emotions from which) Tj T*
(reconstruction had sprung. He was an ardent friend of the reconstruction) Tj T*
(measures. He was convinced of the importance of suppressing the old) Tj T*
(political leaders in his district. He held with enthusiasm the optimistic) Tj T*
(views prevalent in the North regarding the negroes. Their recent progress) Tj T*
(in "education and knowledge," he said, was "marvellous," and if continued,) Tj T*
(in five years the intelligence of the community would shift to the colored) Tj T*
(portion.[99] The purport of his orders, the didactic style in which they) Tj T*
(are couched, the declarations of his principles which frequently accompany) Tj T*
(these orders, indicate the spirit in which he administered the office of) Tj T*
(military governor.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Most of the official acts of Pope concerned either the enforcement of) Tj T*
(obedience and the suppression of disobedience to the letter and spirit of) Tj T*
(the Reconstruction Acts, or the protection and promotion of the present) Tj T*
(interests of the freedmen.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In assuming command he announced that in the absence of special orders all) Tj T*
(persons holding office under the state government would be permitted to) Tj T*
(retain their positions until the expiration of their terms. Their) Tj T*
(successors, however, were to be appointed by Pope alone; no elections) Tj T*
(should be held in the state except those required by Congress. The general) Tj T*
(expressed the hope that no necessity for interference in the regular) Tj T*
(operation of the state government would arise. It could arise, he said,) Tj T*
(only from the failure of state tribunals to do equal justice to all) Tj T*
(persons.[100] A few weeks later he announced that this necessity would) Tj T*
(also arise if any state officer interfered with or opposed the) Tj T*
(reconstruction measures; such an officer, it was "distinctly announced,") Tj T*
(would be deposed.[101] Governor Jenkins, on April 10, had issued a letter) Tj T*
(to the public, advising them to abstain from registering and voting under) Tj T*
(the Reconstruction Acts. Pope had excused him with a lecture, and then) Tj T*
(issued the order referred to, to make clear that no more advice of that) Tj T*
(sort from state officers would be permitted.[102] Opposition to) Tj T*
(reconstruction by state officers was declared to include also the awarding) Tj T*
(of state printing to newspapers which opposed reconstruction, and it was) Tj T*
