(apprehended from the disturbed black population was kindness and friendly) Tj T*
(influence.[127] That opinion was not heard after the arrival of the) Tj T*
(carpet-baggers; its methods were then seen to be inadequate. Secret) Tj T*
(organizations were formed by white men for protection against the negroes.) Tj T*
