(so as to provide that elections held under that legislation should be) Tj T*
(decided by a majority of the votes cast. This act also adopted as part of) Tj T*
(the general scheme two expedients already employed by Pope in the Third) Tj T*
(District. That is to say, it provided that any registered voter might vote) Tj T*
(in any election district in his state, provided he had lived there ten) Tj T*
(days, and that the elections should be "continued from day to day."[134]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
