(citizens at that time. As the negro had no right to hold office because he) Tj T*
(was a citizen, and as he could not claim the right from common law or) Tj T*
(custom, he could obtain it only by specific grant of law. There was no) Tj T*
(such grant. The argument for the negro was made by the Supreme Court of) Tj T*
(the state in 1869, the opposing argument by one of the justices of that) Tj T*
(court in a dissenting opinion.[166]) Tj T*
