(that both houses voted that all were eligible in the face of detailed) Tj T*
(evidence to the contrary, that the decision of the lower house) Tj T*
(contradicted the majority of its committee, and that Meade accepted the) Tj T*
(decision rather for the sake of convenience and finality than because it) Tj T*
(was indisputably correct. On these facts and on some independent) Tj T*
(investigation the Senate judiciary committee based its belief that the) Tj T*
(legislature had failed to obey the Omnibus Act in this respect.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Trumbull, of this committee, submitted a minority report. He admitted that) Tj T*
(the decision of the legislature may have been incorrect. But he protested) Tj T*
(that if the United States government intended to regard the presence of) Tj T*
