(and Congress might correct these two acts by virtue of its power to) Tj T*
(enforce the amendment. If Georgia was not a state, she had not violated) Tj T*
(the Fourteenth Amendment, but her acts were subject to correction by) Tj T*
(Congress, because her government was "provisional only." If, therefore,) Tj T*
(Congress proposed to enforce the Fourteenth Amendment in Georgia, it) Tj T*
(acknowledged that Georgia was a state, and so debarred itself from any) Tj T*
(interference not necessary to enforce that Amendment. If it proposed to) Tj T*
(interfere simply as with a provisional government, there was no such) Tj T*
(limitation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
