(the governor to make one last attempt at prolongation of power. On July 26) Tj T*
(a resolution was offered in the upper house to this effect: That the) Tj T*
(authority of the United States was still paramount in Georgia; that no) Tj T*
(offence ought to be offered to Congress by an apparent denial of this) Tj T*
(fact; that therefore no election should be held in the state until) Tj T*
(Congress had fully recognized its statehood by receiving its) Tj T*
(representatives.[259] On July 29 the senate adopted a resolution similar) Tj T*
(to this, but the lower house rejected it by a few votes.[260] With the) Tj T*
(failure of this attempt, the Reconstruction Acts ceased to operate in) Tj T*
(Georgia, either in fact or in any one's theory.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
