(Humanitarian reforms. The speeches and resolutions show that a close) Tj T*
(sympathy with the Republican party and a bitter antagonism to the) Tj T*
(Conservatives were entertained by most of the members. The temporary) Tj T*
(chairman, Foster Blodgett, in his opening speech, mentioned the) Tj T*
(suspicious, hostile and contemptuous attitude of the Conservatives toward) Tj T*
(the convention. He said:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     They may stand and rail at us and strive to distract us from our) Tj T*
(     patriotic labors; but we are engaged in a great work ... we are) Tj T*
(     building up the walls of a great state.[264]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Parrot, the permanent chairman, said:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     Many of us come here from amongst a people who have spurned us and) Tj T*
(     spit upon us ... the enemies of the convention are watching with) Tj T*
