(     the movements of this body. Our friends will soon be able to) Tj T*
(     determine whether we shall be a burden upon them ... or aid them in) Tj T*
(     the great work of restoring our state.[265]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When Governor Jenkins brought suit against Stanton on behalf of the state,) Tj T*
(the convention declared the action unauthorized and in the name of the) Tj T*
(people of Georgia demanded that the suit be dismissed.[266] On December) Tj T*
(17, 1867, a resolution was passed, asking Pope to appoint, in lieu of) Tj T*
(Governor Jenkins, a provisional governor, and asking that the person) Tj T*
(appointed be Rufus B. Bullock.[267] Unsuccessful here, the convention) Tj T*
